@@ -0,0 +1,157 @@
+# Background music you can actually publish on YouTube
+
+This guide answers one question: **which royalty-free tracks should I keep locally for which kind of video,
+and what licence do they carry?** It is a companion to `music_library/`, the folder the app reads local music
+from, and to `python3 cli.py v3 music-suggest`.
+
+Nothing in this repository re-hosts, bundles or downloads music. You download the files yourself, once, and
+the app reuses them for every video.
+
+---
+
+## 1. The three licences that matter
+
+| Licence | Credit line | Monetised YouTube | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **YouTube Audio Library licence** | Not required for tracks filtered as *Attribution not required* | Yes (YouTube Partner Program) | YouTube states these tracks are copyright-safe and will not be claimed through Content ID. The safety promise is **YouTube-only**. |
+| **Pixabay Content License** | Not required | Yes | Free for commercial use, no royalty. Tracks with a **shield icon are Content ID registered** — avoid those for monetised videos. You may not resell the track as a file. |
+| **CC BY 4.0** (Scott Buckley, Kevin MacLeod, most of Free Music Archive) | **Required**, in the exact published wording, in the video description | Yes | Credit is a licence condition, not a courtesy. Missing it is how CC-BY tracks produce claims. |
+| **CC0 1.0** (Monplaisir and much of Free Music Archive) | Not required | Yes | Public-domain dedication; the simplest option to reuse forever. |
+
+Never use **CC BY-NC** (no commercial use) or **CC BY-ND** (no edits — and ducking/trimming is an edit) on a
+monetised channel. Re-check the licence page before you publish: terms change, and a track you downloaded
+last year may since have been registered with Content ID.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Recommendations by video type
+
+Start with the CC0 track you already have (`Monplaisir - Free To Use 1.ogg`) and add one track per mood, so a
+45-video backlog never repeats the same bed.
+
+### Education, explainers, how-to, habits, wellbeing
+| Track | Artist | Licence | Why |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Free To Use 1 | Monplaisir | CC0 — no credit | Already local. Calm, unobtrusive, survives ducking. Default bed. |
+| Amberlight | Scott Buckley | CC BY 4.0 — credit | Warm piano and strings; hopeful, never sugary. |
+| Life In Motion | Scott Buckley | CC BY 4.0 — credit | Neoclassical and introspective; good under a personal-story opener. |
+| Midvinter | Scott Buckley | CC BY 4.0 — credit | A very gentle piano lullaby; use quietly under slow, calm narration. |
+| Search *"calm piano"* / *"inspiring ambient"* | YouTube Audio Library | filter **Attribution not required** | Zero obligations, four or five usable beds per search. |
+
+### Motivation, self-improvement, discipline
+| Track | Artist | Licence | Why |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Free To Use 1 | Monplaisir | CC0 — no credit | Steady pulse without a drop that fights the narration. |
+| Amberlight | Scott Buckley | CC BY 4.0 — credit | Builds without a hard climax, so the payoff line still lands. |
+| Echoes | Scott Buckley | CC BY 4.0 — credit | Solo cello; use the first half only, before it builds at ~3:10. |
+
+### Documentary, story and cinematic narration
+| Track | Artist | Licence | Why |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Discovery | Scott Buckley | CC BY 4.0 — credit | Optimistic hybrid orchestra; excellent under an opening hook. |
+| Echoes | Scott Buckley | CC BY 4.0 — credit | Emotional strings with a late climax — cut the video around it. |
+| Search *"cinematic documentary"* | Pixabay Music | Content License, no credit | Large choice; check each track for the Content ID shield. |
+
+### Technology, AI and science
+| Track | Artist | Licence | Why |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Origami | Scott Buckley | CC BY 4.0 — credit | Electro-jazz groove; upbeat without being childish. |
+| Discovery | Scott Buckley | CC BY 4.0 — credit | Synth arpeggios read as "future" without a sci-fi cliché. |
+| Search *"technology corporate"* | YouTube Audio Library | filter **Attribution not required** | Clean, neutral beds for tool walk-throughs. |
+
+### Business, finance, career
+| Track | Artist | Licence | Why |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Origami | Scott Buckley | CC BY 4.0 — credit | Confident, not aggressive. |
+| Life In Motion | Scott Buckley | CC BY 4.0 — credit | Credible and human for case studies and interviews. |
+| Search *"corporate motivation"* | Pixabay Music | Content License, no credit | Big library of neutral corporate beds. |
+
+### Kids, cartoons, stories
+| Track | Artist | Licence | Why |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Midvinter | Scott Buckley | CC BY 4.0 — credit | A gentle bed under bedtime-style stories. |
+| Search *"kids playful"* | Pixabay Music | Content License, no credit | Brighter, toy-like beds — pick tracks without the Content ID shield. |
+
+Get the same list in the terminal, with the current URLs:
+
+```bash
+python3 cli.py v3 music-suggest --content-type education
+python3 cli.py v3 music-suggest --content-type documentary --theme cinematic
+python3 cli.py v3 music-suggest --sources          # licence terms per library
+python3 cli.py v3 music-suggest --json             # machine-readable
+```
+
+The credit block to paste into a description is printed with every suggestion, and is also returned as
+`credit_block` in the JSON.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Download once, keep it locally
+
+1. Download the MP3/OGG/WAV from the platform's own page (not from a re-upload — a re-upload has no licence).
+2. Keep the download page URL, the licence name and the artist next to the file (a note or the
+   `music_library/manifest.json` entry does this).
+3. Check the file before importing:
+
+   ```bash
+   python3 cli.py v3 music-check ~/Downloads/ambient-calm.mp3
+   ```
+
+   It prints the size, SHA-256 and a ready-to-fill `manifest.json` snippet, and refuses files that are not
+   playable audio.
+
+4. Import it:
+
+   * **In the app** — Create → **Music library** → upload the file with a title, theme tags, the HTTPS source
+     page and the exact licence label. The app writes `manifest.json` and tags the track.
+   * **By hand** — copy the file into `music_library/` and add an entry to `music_library/manifest.json`:
+
+     ```json
+     {"schema_version": 1, "tracks": [
+       {"file": "ambient-calm.mp3", "sha256": "<from music-check>",
+        "title": "Amberlight", "tags": ["calm", "motivation"],
+        "source_url": "https://www.scottbuckley.com.au/library/amberlight/",
+        "license": "CC BY 4.0 — credit required"}
+     ]}
+     ```
+
+   * **Elsewhere on disk** — point `AUTOVIDEO_MUSIC_LIBRARY` at that folder instead.
+
+5. Tags decide which videos get the track. The library understands `motivation`, `calm`, `upbeat`,
+   `cinematic` and `technology`; `python3 cli.py v3 music-suggest --content-type <type>` prints the tags for
+   that video type.
+
+---
+
+## 4. How the app mixes the music now (v7.0.107)
+
+* The bed starts at the video's `music_volume` (default 0.10–0.12), **fades in** over 1 s and **fades out**
+  over the last 2.5 s instead of stopping dead.
+* While the narrator speaks, a sidechain compressor pulls the bed down by about **13 dB** (12:1 ratio at a
+  0.02 threshold) with a 15 ms attack and a 550 ms release, so the music **returns in every pause**.
+* The finished mix is normalised to **−14 LUFS**, the same target as the English master, so language editions
+  are not quieter than the original.
+* Sound effects are mixed at 0.65 of their planned level so they sit under the voice.
+
+Tune any of it without touching code:
+
+```bash
+python3 cli.py v3 tune <job_id> --show                    # current values
+python3 cli.py v3 tune <job_id> --duck-ratio 16 --duck-release-ms 700
+python3 cli.py v3 tune <job_id> --music-fade-out 4 --sfx-gain 0.5
+python3 cli.py v3 render <job_id>                          # same takes, no Flow credits
+```
+
+If the music still feels loud under speech, raise `--duck-ratio` (12 → 16 → 20) or lower the job's music
+volume. If it feels like it disappears, lower the ratio to 8 and lengthen the fade-out.
+
+---
+
+## 5. A five-minute checklist before publishing
+
+- [ ] Every track is either CC0 / Audio Library *attribution not required* / Pixabay without a shield icon,
+      **or** its exact credit line is in the description.
+- [ ] The credit text was copied from the licence page or the track page, word for word.
+- [ ] No CC BY-NC or CC BY-ND track anywhere.
+- [ ] The track page URL is saved with the file.
+- [ ] The video was uploaded as **Unlisted** first and the Copyright column checked before going public.
